    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 09db5f1d9292fb85de80acc7679623daaae8ce6d -->\n**Needs changes before merge** - one test file does not compile on the merge with current main.\n\n**What looks good**\n- The diff against main is only the burnout commits (2 commits, 18 files); it carries no commits of #1147, #1150, #1158 or #1163.\n- Main's wire verify (#1144) judges the burnout: `WireJob.burnout` turns the slug law into \"must free nothing\" (`crates/sim/src/verify/wire/slug.rs:113`). The pinned golden `wire_burnout_pocket.nc` posts under that law on the trial merge, and the gouging-ring test blocks the post.\n- Refusals are by name (clearance under kerf, no or misplaced start hole, punch side, island split, core left). No unwrap or panic in `burnout.rs`, and the ring count is bounded.\n- The stamp, `EditOperationParams` door and file mirror carry the field. No new dependencies, and no PNG, CHANGELOG or process-file edits.\n\n**Local results (trial merge with main f419d421+)**\n- sim lib 119 pass; motion lib 230 pass (burnout tests included); ui lib 641 pass.\n- app: wire_burnout 3, wire_contour 7, wire_post 7, wire_verify 3, mcp_wire_contour 4, edm_conditions 1, project_roundtrip 73 - all pass.\n- app `wire_readers`: does not compile.\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `burnout` in initializer of `WireContourOp`\n  --> crates\\app\\tests\\wire_readers.rs:67:14\n```\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion, sim and ui clean. app `--all-targets` fails on the same error.\n\n**Requested before merge**\n1. `crates/app/tests/wire_readers.rs:67`: this file is new on main. Add `burnout: None` to the `WireContourOp` literal so the app test target builds again (clippy `--all-targets` and the batch gate need it). Merge main into the branch and make this fix.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The Passes tab gains \"Burn out the pocket (no core)\" and \"Wall clearance\" (`wire_page.rs`). The PR body has no before/after screenshot; please add one.\n- Unexercised, as the body says: a real EDM control, and pockets with islands.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
