    "body": "Merged main (683802be) into the branch to resolve the conflicts from the wire open-run work (#1147 and the other wire PRs).\n\nHand resolutions, all keep-both unless noted:\n- `types/wire_edm.rs`, `project/wire_edm_dto.rs`, `wire_contour.rs`, `wire_post.rs`, `wire_readers.rs`, `wire_verify.rs`: `burnout` (this PR) and `clearance` (main) both kept, in struct, `is_sane`, DTO mirror and test literals.\n- `operation/wire_op.rs`: seed keeps both fields; `generate_wire` takes main's stock + `wire_params(...)` lines, then this PR's `match op.burnout` (burnout / contour) on that `p`.\n- `sim/verify/wire/slug.rs`: main's `CutSide::Open => None` arm kept first and unchanged, then the burnout `Core` arm, then main's other arms untouched.\n- `motion/wire_edm/mod.rs`, `sim/.../tests.rs`, `wire_page.rs`: both exports, both tests, both destructured fields (and main's side combo/clearance row) kept.\n\nFollow-up `fix:` commit: `laws::kerf` gained a closed-ring flag on main, so burnout passes `true`; burnout fixtures and test literals gained main's new `clearance` / `stock` fields (default values).\n\nTests: solid_law_goldens, wire_post, wire_contour, wire_verify, wire_readers, wire_burnout (app) all green; motion wire_edm (13) and sim wire (7) green; clippy -D warnings clean on motion, sim, app, ui. No golden or snapshot changed.\n\nA delta review of this merge follows.\n",
