    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: a8b404463f22c48bd113b5492ecc568d6d42807f -->\nDelta review of head a8b4044 (main merged since the clean review at 5e5e5ae, plus the `fix:` commit). Ready for the maintainer to merge.\n\n**Checked**\n- `git diff origin/main --stat` lists only the PR's own 20 files; nothing from main is dropped.\n- `wire_op.rs` `generate_wire`: main's stock and `wire_params` lines are intact; the burnout `match` follows them, so burnout programs still reach main's door, kerf and verify path. `clearance_door` is added in `condition_of`.\n- `slug.rs`: main's `CutSide::Open => None` arm is unchanged and first; the burnout `Core` arm comes next, then main's `NothingFreed` / Die / Punch arms. Every case main refuses with `burnout == false` still refuses. The sim wire law files are not byte-identical to main (the PR adds `WireJob.burnout`, `WireFinding::Core` and that arm), but additively.\n- `fix:` commit: `laws::kerf(path, given, given_closed, k, z)` (laws.rs:118). `true` means the given profile is a closed ring, the same as the contour call at mod.rs:232. The kerf floor is not weakened. Test fixtures take default `clearance`/`stock` values.\n- `wire_page.rs`, `wire_edm_dto.rs`, `types/wire_edm.rs`: `burnout` sits beside main's `clearance`. The DTO field is `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if)]`, so existing project files are unchanged. The params stamp writes `burnout` only when set.\n\n**Local results (merged with main, own target)**\n- app: solid_law_goldens 6, wire_burnout 3, wire_contour 8, wire_post 8, wire_readers 7, wire_verify 3, all pass\n- motion wire_edm 13 pass; sim wire tests 7 pass; ui lib wire 4 pass\n- clippy `-D warnings` on motion, sim, app, ui (all targets): clean\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\n**Notes:** no UI screenshots in the body for the new wire page rows (note only).\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
